From af091dd395fdf4195dd356855d477d5f19bac281 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 04:19:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Cashier & Payment Method report with Excel/PDF export

New self-contained section on the Reports page (its own filters,
independent of the main summary's date range above it):

- app/models/Report.php: cashiersWithSales() (only cashiers who
  actually rang up a sale in the range, for the dropdown),
  cashierName(), and cashierPaymentBreakdown() - revenue grouped by
  cashier AND payment method, optionally narrowed to one cashier
  and/or one payment method. Reads from SalePayments rather than
  Sales.payment_method for the same reason paymentBreakdown() already
  does - a split-payment sale would otherwise dump entirely into an
  unhelpful 'MULTIPLE' bucket.
- app/controllers/ReportController.php: cashier_payment_breakdown
  (JSON, for the on-page table), export_cashier_payment_excel and
  export_cashier_payment_pdf (separate buttons/endpoints per the
  request) - both reuse the existing dependency-free XlsxWriter/
  PdfWriter helpers already used by the Item Ledger and Sales exports.
- views/reports.php, assets/js/reports.js: cashier select (auto-
  populated from sales in range), payment method select, date presets
  (Today/Yesterday/This Week/This Month) plus a custom date-range
  pair, a small summary strip, and the breakdown table.
